Service check
The one call that needs no credentials. Make it first: if it answers, the address is right and your network can reach us, so anything failing after this is the keys or the request — not the connection.

GET
/ping
Are you there? No API key needed.
Response
{
    "status": 200,
    "message": "pong",
    "service": "steadfast-api",
    "version": "v1",
    "time": "2026-09-20T13:45:09+06:00"
}
The only endpoint that takes no credentials, which is the point of it: everywhere else a wrong key, a wrong base URL, a firewall and a proxy that drops your headers all look identical — 401. If ping answers and the rest does not, the problem is your credentials.
It says we are reachable. It does not say your keys work — for that call GET /get_balance, which is cheap and answers 401 if they do not.
It never touches our database or queues and reports nothing about them, so a 200 here is not a promise that booking is healthy. Use it as a connectivity check, not as a monitor for our service.
`time` is ISO 8601 with our offset (Asia/Dhaka). Compare it with your own clock — a skewed clock is behind a surprising number of "why is my parcel dated tomorrow" questions.
Rate limited by IP like everything else, so do not poll it in a tight loop.
Authentication
Headers on every request
Api-Key
Your API key.
Secret-Key
Your secret key.
Content-Type
application/json on POST.
There is no login step and no token to refresh. Send both keys on every call.

When it goes wrong
Missing or wrong credentials answer 401. Repeated failures from one address and key are counted: after 10 in five minutes you are refused with 429 for 60 minutes, correct keys included. Do not retry a 401 in a loop — fix the keys first.

Rate limits are 1,000 requests a minute, and 6,000 for booking.

Keys belong to one profile
If you run more than one business with us, each has its own keys. A key issued for a business books parcels onto that business and can read only that business's parcels and payouts — it cannot see your main account's, and your main account's key cannot see the business's. That is what makes a key safe to hand to one shop's developer.

You can hold several keys in each profile: one per integration, named, so that retiring your old plugin does not take your ERP down with it. Issue and revoke them on
Your API keys
.

Two things that surprise people
We strip some characters. Before storing an address, a name or a note we replace each of {</code> <code>}</code> <code>;</code> <code><</code> <code>></code> <code>$ with a space. Text you send is not always text you get back.

We truncate rather than refuse. Over-long values are cut to fit:

invoice	100 characters
recipient_name	100 characters
recipient_phone	40 characters
recipient_address	490 characters
note	480 characters
Check your own lengths if the exact value matters to you.

Booking parcels
Creating a parcel is the one call most integrations make. Everything else answers questions about parcels you already booked.

POST
/create_order
Book one parcel.
Fields
Field	Type	What it is
invoiceRequired	string	Your own order number. Letters, digits, hyphens and underscores only. Must not repeat one you have already used — that is what makes a retry safe. Stored to 100 characters.
recipient_nameRequired	string	Stored to 100 characters.
recipient_phoneRequired	string	Eleven digits beginning 01.
recipient_addressRequired	string	Stored to 490 characters.
cod_amountRequired	number	What to collect on delivery, in BDT. 0 for a prepaid order. Maximum 1,000,000.
noteOptional	string	Delivery instructions for the rider. Up to 480 characters.
alternative_phoneOptional	string	A second number to try. Eleven digits beginning 01.
recipient_emailOptional	string	Must be a deliverable address — the domain is checked.
item_descriptionOptional	string	What is in the parcel. Up to 255 characters.
total_lotOptional	number	How many items. Defaults to 1.
delivery_typeOptional	number	0 for home delivery (the default), 1 for point delivery.
exchangeOptional	boolean	true to book an exchange parcel — the rider delivers this one and brings back the item being exchanged. Defaults to false. Send `true` / `false` in JSON, or `"true"` / `"false"` (or 1 / 0) in a form.
Request
{
    "invoice": "ORD-10231",
    "recipient_name": "Jahid Hasan",
    "recipient_phone": "01712345678",
    "recipient_address": "House 17/1, Road 3/A, Dhanmondi, Dhaka-1209",
    "cod_amount": 1060,
    "note": "Call before 3 PM"
}
Response
{
    "status": 200,
    "message": "Consignment has been created successfully.",
    "consignment": {
        "consignment_id": 1424107,
        "invoice": "ORD-10231",
        "tracking_code": "15BAEB8A",
        "tracking_link": "https://steadfast.com.bd/tl/a1b2c3d4",
        "recipient_name": "Jahid Hasan",
        "recipient_phone": "01712345678",
        "recipient_address": "House 17/1, Road 3/A, Dhanmondi, Dhaka-1209",
        "recipient_email": null,
        "alternative_phone": null,
        "item_description": null,
        "total_lot": 1,
        "cod_amount": 1060,
        "exchange": false,
        "status": "in_review",
        "note": "Call before 3 PM",
        "created_at": "2026-09-20T07:05:31.000000Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-09-20T07:05:31.000000Z"
