            "tracking_code": null,
            "status": null,
            "error": "[\"THIS_INVOICE_ALREADY_EXISTS\"]"
        }
    ]
}
Error codes
INVOICE_IS_REQUIRED	No `invoice` on this order.
INVOICE_MUST_BE_ALPHA_NUM_DASH_UNDERSCORE	The invoice has a character other than a letter, digit, hyphen or underscore.
INVOICE_LENGTH_SHOULD_BE_LESS_THAN_100_CHARS	The invoice is too long.
THIS_INVOICE_ALREADY_EXISTS	You have already booked a parcel with this invoice.
RECEIVER_NAME_IS_REQUIRED	No `recipient_name`.
RECEIVER_NAME_LENGTH_SHOULD_BE_LESS_THAN_100_CHARS	The name is too long.
RECEIVER_PHONE_IS_REQUIRED	No `recipient_phone`.
RECEIVER_PHONE_LENGTH_SHOULD_BE_LESS_THAN_40_CHARS	The phone number is too long.
RECEIVER_ADDRESS_IS_REQUIRED	No `recipient_address`.
RECEIVER_ADDRESS_LENGTH_SHOULD_BE_LESS_THAN_500_CHARS	The address is too long.
RECEIVER_NOTE_LENGTH_SHOULD_BE_LESS_THAN_500_CHARS	The note is too long.
COD_AMOUNT_ERROR	No `cod_amount` on this order.
ERROR	`cod_amount` is not a number.
EXCHANGE_MUST_BE_TRUE_OR_FALSE	`exchange` is something other than true or false.
The whole request answers 200 even when some orders failed. Read every entry.
`data` comes back in the order you sent it, one entry per order, so you can match results to your own rows by position as well as by `invoice`.
A successful entry carries `status: "success"` and a `consignment_id`. A failed one carries `status: null` and `error`, a JSON-encoded array of codes.
Partial success is normal and is not an error: book the failures again after fixing them, leaving the successes alone.
Mark an order as an exchange with `exchange: true` on that order. Orders without it are booked as ordinary parcels.
