Parcels move between states while they are being worked, so paging through a busy state can show a parcel twice or miss one that has just moved on. Read the list again later to catch up.
Stats
The figures on your Stats page: how the parcels you booked in a date range turned out, and the cash on delivery in each outcome.

GET
/stats
Counts and COD per outcome for the parcels you booked between two dates.
Fields
Field	Type	What it is
fromOptional	string (query)	First day, `YYYY-MM-DD`. Defaults to 30 days ago.
toOptional	string (query)	Last day, `YYYY-MM-DD`, counted in full. Defaults to today.
Response
{
    "status": 200,
    "from": "2026-10-01",
    "to": "2026-10-31",
    "total": {
        "count": 412,
        "cod_amount": 628450
    },
    "success_rate": 84,
    "cancel_rate": 9,
    "delivered": {
        "count": 331,
        "cod_amount": 512300,
        "share": 80
    },
    "partial": {
        "count": 16,
        "cod_amount": 21400,
        "share": 4
    },
    "cancelled": {
        "count": 37,
        "cod_amount": 52650,
        "share": 9
    },
    "pending": {
        "count": 21,
        "cod_amount": 33900,
        "share": 5
    },
    "approval": {
        "count": 7,
        "cod_amount": 8200,
        "share": 2
    }
}
Parcels are counted by the day they were booked. Each falls in exactly one outcome: `delivered`, `partial` (partly delivered), `cancelled`, `pending` (with the rider) or `approval` (the rider has delivered it and it is waiting for our approval).
Parcels still in review or on hold are not counted.
`success_rate` is delivered plus partly delivered as a percentage of `total`; `cancel_rate` and each `share` are percentages of `total`, rounded.
Any range works, back to your first parcel — older parcels are included even after they have been archived.
